```spl
/*
===================================================================
SPL QUERY: PowerShell Execution, Scripting Triage & Telemetry Gaps
File: splunk/powershell-investigation.spl
Target Events: Sysmon Event ID 1 (powershell.exe), PowerShell Event IDs 4104 (Script Block) / 4103
Sourcetypes: XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational, WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-PowerShell/Operational, _json
===================================================================

1. INVESTIGATION OBJECTIVE:
   Identify suspicious PowerShell processes, flag obfuscation, evasion arguments
   (-enc, -nop, -w hidden, -ep bypass), inspect command lines for recon cmdlets
   (Get-NetTCPConnection, Invoke-WebRequest, IEX), and evaluate telemetry gaps when
   Script Block Logging (Event 4104) is absent or disabled.

2. REQUIRED FIELDS:
   - Sysmon Event 1: Image, CommandLine, ParentImage, ParentProcessId, ProcessId, User, LogonId.
   - PowerShell Event 4104 (if present): ScriptBlockText, Path.
*/

index=* (EventCode=1 OR EventID=1 OR EventCode=4104 OR EventID=4104) (Image="*powershell.exe*" OR process_name="powershell.exe" OR Channel="*PowerShell*")
| eval ProcessPath=coalesce(Image, process_path)
| eval ExecutedCommand=coalesce(CommandLine, ScriptBlockText, Message)
| eval ParentBinary=coalesce(ParentImage, parent_process_path)
| eval UserContext=coalesce(User, user)
| eval TargetSession=coalesce(LogonId, "Unknown")
| eval EvasionIndicator=case(
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)-ExecutionPolicy\s+(Bypass|Unrestricted)"), "ExecutionPolicy Bypass",
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)(-w(indowstyle)?\s+hidden)"), "Hidden Window Execution",
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)(-enc(odedcommand)?)"), "Base64 Encoded Command",
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)(-nop(rofile)?)"), "No Profile Loaded",
    true(), "Standard / Unflagged"
  )
| eval ReconIndicator=case(
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)Get-NetTCPConnection"), "Network Connection Enumeration",
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)(Invoke-WebRequest|Net\.WebClient|curl|wget)"), "Web Retrieval / Staging",
    match(ExecutedCommand, "(?i)IEX|Invoke-Expression"), "Dynamic Code Execution",
    true(), "General Command"
  )
| table _time, EventCode, UserContext, TargetSession, ParentBinary, ProcessPath, EvasionIndicator, ReconIndicator, ExecutedCommand
| sort - _time

/*
===================================================================
3. EXPECTED OUTPUT ON SYNTHETIC DATASET:
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   _time                EventCode UserContext TargetSession ParentBinary         ProcessPath             EvasionIndicator        ReconIndicator
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   2026-10-24 14:25:30  1         LAB\jdoe    0x14A28F      C:\...\cmd.exe       C:\...\powershell.exe   ExecutionPolicy Bypass  Network Connection Enumeration
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4. TELEMETRY GAP DOCUMENTATION:
   - Observation: In our synthetic dataset, Sysmon Event ID 1 captured the full CLI argument:
     powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -NoProfile -WindowStyle Hidden -Command "Get-NetTCPConnection | Where-Object {$_.State -eq 'Listen'} | Out-File C:\Users\Public\net_recon.txt"
   - Telemetry Gap: If an adversary uses Base64 encoded commands (`-enc <base64>`) or executes scripts from files,
     Sysmon Event 1 shows only the encoded blob or file path (`powershell.exe -File script.ps1`).
   - Prerequisite Fix: In an enterprise baseline, Group Policy must enforce:
     * Computer Configuration -> Administrative Templates -> Windows Components -> Windows PowerShell:
       1. Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging (Generates Event ID 4104, capturing decoded executable code).
       2. Turn on PowerShell Transcription (Logs all I/O to a protected centralized share).

5. MITRE ATT&CK MAPPING:
   - T1059.001 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell
   - T1562.001 - Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools (Execution Policy Bypass)
   - T1049 - System Network Connections Discovery
===================================================================
*/
```
